exports[`triage handoff template snapshots > triage to planner renders the complete contract 1`] = `
"> ⚠️ **Template notice — not part of the message. Do not copy this notice into your handoff.**
> Recipient visibility: the \`planner\` agent receives only the text inside your \`handoff --next-role="planner"\` command. It cannot see anything you write in this agent session, or tool output. Put your complete deliverable in the handoff message.

Instructions (not part of the message): Return a complete, evidence-backed investigation of the authoritative reported bug. Triage is advisory: do not edit implementation files or implement the proposed fix. Begin with the \`## Summary\` section, then use the remaining sections below in order. Use \`###\` for sub-items within a section. Cite concrete repository paths and symbols, observed behavior, commands, and test output. Distinguish confirmed findings from hypotheses; never claim a test proved behavior unless its failing assertion demonstrates the report.

Message template for \`planner\` (copy only the body sections below; do not copy this line, the notice, or the instructions after the body):

## Summary
<briefly state the diagnosis and whether the root cause was confirmed or remains a hypothesis>

## Reported behavior
<state the reported symptoms and expected behavior, including reproduction details and constraints recovered from the request or relevant history>

## Root cause
<trace the relevant ownership, data, and control flow using concrete repository paths and symbols; explain the causal reasoning and explicitly label the finding as confirmed or a hypothesis>

## Reproduction attempt
<give the focused test path and exact command, the failing assertion or exact blocker, and the outcome; if reproduction was blocked, state what was tried and what additional information would help; do not fabricate proof>

## Proposed immediate fix
<recommend the smallest appropriate change, naming the likely files and the specific change; do not implement it>

## Systemic issues
<list each separate systemic concern with repository evidence, impact, and follow-up concern, or write exactly: None observed.>

## Work completed
<state the code paths inspected and every test or reproduction action taken, including results>

Instructions after the body (not part of the message): run the normal handoff command to \`planner\` with the complete body above, then stop.

\`\`\`bash
chatroom handoff --chatroom-id="<chatroom-id>" --role="triage" --next-role="planner" << 'CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END'
---MESSAGE---
[Your message here]
CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END
\`\`\`"
`;

